From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 06:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] s3torchconnectorclient: ship the licences of the statically
 linked dependencies

The wheel's native extension statically links the AWS Common Runtime
(aws-lc, s2n-tls, aws-c-common, aws-c-cal, aws-c-io, aws-c-compression,
aws-c-http, aws-c-sdkutils, aws-c-auth, aws-checksums, aws-c-s3) via
mountpoint-s3-crt-sys, but the explicit license-files list only ships
this project's own LICENSE/NOTICE: THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES is generated
by upstream's own ORT-based CI job and is not checked into the repo,
so it never exists in a plain checkout. Drop that entry and match
LICENSE.* instead, where the build stages each vendored dependency's
licence text next to pyproject.toml.

Upstream-Status: To upstream [this port does not open issues/PRs against third-party repos; the upstream wheels have the same THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES generation step and gap when built from a plain checkout]
---
 s3torchconnectorclient/pyproject.toml | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/s3torchconnectorclient/pyproject.toml b/s3torchconnectorclient/pyproject.toml
index 8542d48..2a0cce0 100644
--- a/s3torchconnectorclient/pyproject.toml
+++ b/s3torchconnectorclient/pyproject.toml
@@ -45,7 +45,7 @@ find = { where = ["python/src"] }
 target = "s3torchconnectorclient._mountpoint_s3_client"
 
 [tool.setuptools]
-license-files = [ "LICENSE", "THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES", "NOTICE"]
+license-files = [ "LICENSE", "NOTICE", "LICENSE.*"]
 
 [tool.cibuildwheel]
 test-requires = ["./s3torchconnector[test,e2e]"]
